        "note": "The note uses the scholastic distinction between lux (light as it is in the shining source) and lumen (light spread through the medium). English has only one word for both, so the translation says 'source of light' for lux. 'Act' is the Aristotelian actuality: the transparent medium is made actually transparent by light. This echoes Aristotle's definition of light in De anima, but the wording here is a school formula.",
